% Cinder (elemental chemistry)
%
% A fire imp, wreathed in flame, holds the cloister yard. Things of fire
% freeze solid when chilled - but cold on a burning thing only quenches the
% flame. Put the fire out first, then freeze it. The cloister keeps a
% fountain (a basin nobody can walk into) and a frozen pond. Two
% companions, one skill each, from a pool of eight.
%
%   court (player, mage) ---- yard (imp: fire, burning)
%     |      \                  |  \
%   cloister   (sees)        fountain (puddle; only a push lands there)
%     |
%   pond (iceSheet: whoever arrives is chilled)   gate (off the yard)
%
% Obstacles:
%   burning    cold on it quenches the flame instead of freezing it (quench)
%   fire       fire on it does nothing (immune to burning)
%   a spilled zone does not land again where it already lies: a second
%   cold spell on the same ice does nothing
%
% Methods (each needs two different companions):
%   douse, then chill   rain or a wave puts the fire out (extinguish);
%                       then frost (glaciate, iceStorm) freezes it
%   quench, then drag   anything wet or cold puts the fire out; then
%                       someone on the frozen pond drags it onto the ice
%                       (magnetize) or trades places with it (translocate)
%   dunk, then freeze   a blast from the court throws it into the fountain
%                       (gust; fireball, whose fire does nothing to it but
%                       whose blast still lands), which puts the fire out;
%                       then frost it there, or drag it out onto the ice
%
% Traps:
%   frost first only quenches it, and the ice then lies under it: a second
%   frost there does nothing. Dragging it onto the pond first quenches it
%   on the ice, and it cannot arrive there again. A wave that soaks it also
%   throws it into the fountain - that is fine, it is still only wet.
%   Rain after frost only wets it. Nothing sees the pond, so once the imp
%   stands on the ice, nobody can bring it there a second time.
%
% Not in the pool: taunt. Its pull comes from onGrant(taunted, pull), which
% the engine applies raw, so a taunted imp dragged onto the ice skips the
% quench and freezes while still burning - one skill, one companion.

% === Regions ===
region(court).
region(yard).
region(fountain).
region(cloister).
region(pond).
region(gate).
connected(court, yard).
connected(yard, court).
connected(yard, gate).
connected(gate, yard).
connected(court, cloister).
connected(cloister, court).
connected(cloister, pond).
connected(pond, cloister).
lineOfSight(court, yard).
lineOfSight(court, fountain).
lineOfSight(pond, yard).
lineOfSight(pond, fountain).

% Push line: from the court, the yard tips into the fountain.
beyond(court, yard, fountain).

% === Zones ===
onEnter(fountain, puddle).
onEnter(pond, iceSheet).

% === Companions ===
role(player, player).
role(mage, companion).
at(player, court).
at(mage, court).
mana(player, 4).
mana(mage, 4).

% === Enemy ===
role(imp, enemy).
at(imp, yard).
element(imp, fire).
tag(imp, burning).

% === Default kit: one skill each (combos replans the whole matrix) ===
knows(player, rainCall).
knows(mage, glaciate).

% === The goal: the imp freezes ===
win :- if(), do(neutralize(imp)).
win :- if(), do(putOutAndFreeze(imp)).

% The fire goes out (by one companion), then the cold lands (by the other).
putOutAndFreeze(?e) :-
    if(holds(?e, burning), canAct(?p)),
    do(putOut(?p, ?e), ensureOff(burning, ?e), freeze(?e, ?p), confirmStopped(?e)).

% Water or cold on it - cast, or a push into water - or a drag onto it.
putOut(?p, ?e) :- if(), do(primeAs(?p, wet, ?e)).
putOut(?p, ?e) :- if(zoneFor(?r, wet)), do(pullOnto(?p, ?e, ?r)).

% Cold on it - cast, or a drag onto the ice - by anyone but ?not.
freeze(?e, ?not) :- if(), do(inflict(chilled, ?e, ?not)).
freeze(?e, ?not) :-
    if(canAct(?a), \==(?a, ?not), zoneFor(?r, chilled)), do(pullOnto(?a, ?e, ?r)).

% ?a, standing in ?r, brings ?e there: drags it, or trades places with it.
pullOnto(?a, ?e, ?r) :-
    if(puller(?a, ?ab, ?e), at(?e, ?er), \==(?er, ?r), reach(?ab, ?k), inRange(?k, ?r, ?er),
       canReachNow(?a, ?r)),
    do(castFrom(?a, ?ab, ?e, ?r)).
pullOnto(?a, ?e, ?r) :-
    if(canAct(?a), knows(?a, ?ab), effect(?ab, target, swap), ready(?a, ?ab, ?e), at(?e, ?er), \==(?er, ?r),
       reach(?ab, ?k), inRange(?k, ?r, ?er), canReachNow(?a, ?r)),
    do(castFrom(?a, ?ab, ?e, ?r)).

funExpect(single_actor_plans, atMost, 0).

% === Choice: one skill each, from eight (htn_components combos) ===
comboSeat(player, 1).
comboSeat(mage, 1).
comboPool(rainCall).
comboPool(tidalWave).
comboPool(glaciate).
comboPool(iceStorm).
comboPool(gust).
comboPool(fireball).
comboPool(magnetize).
comboPool(translocate).
comboMinWins(4).
comboMinMethods(3).

goals(win).
